Notes on real data (Case 1):
- 7 of 8 days have unpriced requests (unpriced=8..537), so the PR's gate withholds cost and shares use the token
  basis; the tile's 94% / 5% / 1% are token shares. Top-3 tokens sum 293,024,190 of 293,761,113 total (a 4th model
  holds the remaining ~0.25%); shares divide by all models.
- Real history was fully scanned (historyScanIsPartial=false, historyIsFullyScanned=true), so ClawSweeper P2 #1
  (partial scan not withheld) was NOT exercised by this data. Breakdown sums matched every day's totals exactly
  (coverage 1.0000), so P2 #2 did not show on real data either.
- Case 3 (synthetic) reproduces P2 #2 through the full store -> JSON -> tile path: a day whose sole breakdown covers
  40% of its tokens and cost is published as 100% for that model.
- The provider mark renders as the "CL" initials fallback: the harness does not compile the asset catalog (no actool).

Installed WidgetKit extension: NOT exercised.
- Scripts/package_app.sh builds CodexBarWidget.appex only via xcodegen + `xcodebuild -scheme CodexBarWidgetExtension`
  (lines ~471-548); this Mac has no Xcode (`xcrun --find actool` fails; xcodebuild unavailable). SwiftPM's
  `CodexBarWidget` executable product is not a WidgetKit .appex bundle.
- The registered widget on this Mac (pluginkit: com.steipete.codexbar.widget 0.83.0) is the released app, which
  predates the topModels field, so it cannot show PR behavior.
- Hence: in-process rendering of the production SwiftUI tile from the persisted/decoded snapshot, not a WidgetKit
  host. Timeline provider, app-group container I/O and reloadAllTimelines were not exercised.
